# 4. Architectural Principles

The simulator must follow these principles:

1. Account balances must be transactionally consistent.
2. Every balance-changing operation must have a ledger entry.
3. Every reservation must be idempotent.
4. Every settlement must be idempotent.
5. Duplicate messages must not create duplicate financial changes.
6. Every important state transition must be auditable.
7. Current balance must be reconcilable from transaction history.
8. Test behavior must be deterministic when configured.
9. Failures and delays must be configurable.
10. The simulator must support concurrent requests safely.
11. No financial state should depend only on in-memory state.
12. Simulator restarts must not lose account or reservation state.
13. Test data must be easily resettable.
14. Business rules must be configurable where the real downstream contract is not yet finalized.

